{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WECJ6hA3jHz9XBdhYTNU8y","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Construction-first remedies: wire the antidote doctrine into the reviewer's finding contract\n2\t\n3\t**Status:** plan of record for the row minted against it. Authored 2026-09-01\n4\tfrom the supervised-unpause run's measured review/rework interplay (the log's\n5\t2026-09-01 entry; delegated decisions 47–51).\n6\t\n7\t## 1. The problem, measured\n8\t\n9\tAcross thirteen REVIEW-A rounds on five rows, **one** remedy was structural.\n10\tEvery other finding's remedy was additive — \"wire the checker\", \"extend the\n11\tinvariant\", \"add a regression test\", \"add a warn\". The exception is WI-543\n12\tround 2, which demanded the delivered universe be *enumerated and diffed*\n13\trather than checked; the result (`bootstrap.delivery_inventory()`) makes an\n14\tomitted shipped file **unrepresentable** instead of detected, and it is the\n15\thealthiest change in the run.\n16\t\n17\tThe clearest accretion trace is the successor invariant:\n18\t\n19\t1. It gated on the `brief` cell. WI-552 round 1 found the cancelled arm is\n20\t   brief-less by design, so the guard was blind to it.\n21\t2. The fix re-keyed it to a **title-string prefix**\n22\t   (`intake.owes_successor`, `title.startswith(\"dispose:\")`), enforced in\n23\t   **two** places — `handback.close_adjudication` and\n24\t   `intake._disposition_drafts` — the second because an agent may self-close\n25\t   past the first.\n26\t3. WI-566's round then found the predictable consequence: an `adjudicate:`\n27\t   title carrying an `amendment` brief slips **both** guards. The remedy\n28\t   proposed for that was \"extend the invariant (or a warn)\" — a third guard\n29\t   on the same axis.\n30\t\n31\tThe construction alternative is visible in the code and nobody in the chain\n32\tproposed it: `intake._close_drafts` **knows** which arm it is minting (an\n33\texplicit `outcome == \"cancelled\"` branch), encodes that fact into a title\n34\tstring, and omits the typed cell — after which two guards sniff it back out\n35\tby prefix. A typed obligation cell written at the mint, which the close\n36\tcannot drift from, retires the whole class.\n37\t\n38\t**Why the bias persists — it is economic, not intellectual.** Complying with\n39\ta finding costs the lane zero extra rounds; disputing one costs a round and\n40\trisks another CHANGES-REQUESTED. Implementers in this run were otherwise\n41\tdiscriminating (WI-552's two MINORs were queued rather than patched inline —\n42\t`intake._OI_ID_RE` is still dead at intake.py:304; WI-566's rework refused a\n43\tremedy outright and *proved* with `parse_dispositions` that it would halt the\n44\tmerge sweep). The asymmetry is in what the reviewer is asked to produce, so\n45\tthat is where to fix it.\n46\t\n47\t## 2. What this is NOT\n48\t\n49\t- **Not new doctrine.** The rule already ships: the vendored `antidote`\n50\t  skill (`scope: kit`) — \"What is the smallest change that makes this fix\n51\t  unnecessary?\" — with PROCESS.md §3's 0→A→B rule as its repo-scale form.\n52\t  State it once, reference it; do not restate it in the prompt\n53\t  (`CLAUDE.md`, \"Dogfood the philosophy\").\n54\t- **Not a gate.** No finding is refused, downgraded, or blocked for lacking\n55\t  the justification. Warn-first doctrine: the discipline is on the remedy's\n56\t  *wording*, not on the verdict or any exit code.\n57\t- **Not \"reviewers must design the fix.\"** Naming why construction is\n58\t  unavailable is cheap; specifying the structural change is not the\n59\t  reviewer's job when it exceeds the diff's scope.\n60\t- **Not an argument against guards.** Validation at trust boundaries stays\n61\t  (the antidote skill says so itself, and the kit's own fail-closed reads —\n62\t  an absent OI is NOT satisfied — are correct by construction, not\n63\t  defensive accretion). The target is the guard that compensates for a\n64\t  *reachable* bad state the design could have made unreachable.\n65\t\n66\t## 3. Done-when\n67\t\n68\t1. `project-trajectory/prompts/reviewer.template.md`'s finding-line contract\n69\t   requires, for any remedy that adds a check, guard, warn, or invariant,\n70\t   one clause naming why the defect cannot be made unrepresentable instead\n71\t   (stricter type, deleted path, single owning boundary) — citing the\n72\t   `antidote` skill rather than restating it. The MINOR/`for clarity` arm\n73\t   and trust-boundary validation are explicitly exempt.\n74\t2. `project-trajectory/prompts/CATALOG.md` regenerated\n75\t   (`gen_prompt_catalog.py`); the `REVIEWER` digest is the join key a\n76\t   session log's `prompt-sha` names, so a stale catalog is a red bar.\n77\t3. A test in `tests/test_prompts.py` pins the clause's presence, in that\n78\t   module's existing style (it already guards 33 prompt-template\n79\t   properties).\n80\t4. The same discipline reaches the adjudicator briefs if and only if it\n81\t   applies there — read `adjudicate_brief.py`'s templates before deciding;\n82\t   do not widen by reflex, which would be this plan's own failure mode.\n83\t5. Recorded so the effect is measurable: the fragment states the\n84\t   structural-vs-additive remedy split of the 2026-09-01 run (1 of 13) as\n85\t   the baseline a later sitting re-measures against.\n86\t\n87\t## 4. Evidence trail\n88\t\n89\tThe run's rounds are under `docs/reviews/wi-543-*`, `wi-552-*`, `wi-553-*`,\n90\t`wi-563-*`, `wi-566-*`; the interplay analysis and the accretion trace are\n91\tin the log's 2026-09-01 supervised-unpause entry and decisions 47–51. The\n92\tamendment-arm gap named in §1 step 3 is recorded there as an unfiled kit\n93\tfinding and is NOT this row's to fix — this row changes what future rounds\n94\tare asked to produce.\n95\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d1f7b81f-b88d-4166-875f-573dc007de72","uuid":"c28d5cb4-d582-4e04-92ac-cb06525ba11c","timestamp":"2026-09-01T19:40:21.062Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template-drive/wi-567-construction-first-remedies-t/docs/plans/2026-09-01-construction-first-remedies.md","content":"# Construction-first remedies: wire the antidote doctrine into the reviewer's finding contract\n\n**Status:** plan of record for the row minted against it. Authored 2026-09-01\nfrom the supervised-unpause run's measured review/rework interplay (the log's\n2026-09-01 entry; delegated decisions 47–51).\n\n## 1. The problem, measured\n\nAcross thirteen REVIEW-A rounds on five rows, **one** remedy was structural.\nEvery other finding's remedy was additive — \"wire the checker\", \"extend the\ninvariant\", \"add a regression test\", \"add a warn\". The exception is WI-543\nround 2, which demanded the delivered universe be *enumerated and diffed*\nrather than checked; the result (`bootstrap.delivery_inventory()`) makes an\nomitted shipped file **unrepresentable** instead of detected, and it is the\nhealthiest change in the run.\n\nThe clearest accretion trace is the successor invariant:\n\n1. It gated on the `brief` cell. WI-552 round 1 found the cancelled arm is\n   brief-less by design, so the guard was blind to it.\n2. The fix re-keyed it to a **title-string prefix**\n   (`intake.owes_successor`, `title.startswith(\"dispose:\")`), enforced in\n   **two** places — `handback.close_adjudication` and\n   `intake._disposition_drafts` — the second because an agent may self-close\n   past the first.\n3. WI-566's round then found the predictable consequence: an `adjudicate:`\n   title carrying an `amendment` brief slips **both** guards. The remedy\n   proposed for that was \"extend the invariant (or a warn)\" — a third guard\n   on the same axis.\n\nThe construction alternative is visible in the code and nobody in the chain\nproposed it: `intake._close_drafts` **knows** which arm it is minting (an\nexplicit `outcome == \"cancelled\"` branch), encodes that fact into a title\nstring, and omits the typed cell — after which two guards sniff it back out\nby prefix. A typed obligation cell written at the mint, which the close\ncannot drift from, retires the whole class.\n\n**Why the bias persists — it is economic, not intellectual.** Complying with\na finding costs the lane zero extra rounds; disputing one costs a round and\nrisks another CHANGES-REQUESTED. Implementers in this run were otherwise\ndiscriminating (WI-552's two MINORs were queued rather than patched inline —\n`intake._OI_ID_RE` is still dead at intake.py:304; WI-566's rework refused a\nremedy outright and *proved* with `parse_dispositions` that it would halt the\nmerge sweep). The asymmetry is in what the reviewer is asked to produce, so\nthat is where to fix it.\n\n## 2. What this is NOT\n\n- **Not new doctrine.** The rule already ships: the vendored `antidote`\n  skill (`scope: kit`) — \"What is the smallest change that makes this fix\n  unnecessary?\" — with PROCESS.md §3's 0→A→B rule as its repo-scale form.\n  State it once, reference it; do not restate it in the prompt\n  (`CLAUDE.md`, \"Dogfood the philosophy\").\n- **Not a gate.** No finding is refused, downgraded, or blocked for lacking\n  the justification. Warn-first doctrine: the discipline is on the remedy's\n  *wording*, not on the verdict or any exit code.\n- **Not \"reviewers must design the fix.\"** Naming why construction is\n  unavailable is cheap; specifying the structural change is not the\n  reviewer's job when it exceeds the diff's scope.\n- **Not an argument against guards.** Validation at trust boundaries stays\n  (the antidote skill says so itself, and the kit's own fail-closed reads —\n  an absent OI is NOT satisfied — are correct by construction, not\n  defensive accretion). The target is the guard that compensates for a\n  *reachable* bad state the design could have made unreachable.\n\n## 3. Done-when\n\n1. `project-trajectory/prompts/reviewer.template.md`'s finding-line contract\n   requires, for any remedy that adds a check, guard, warn, or invariant,\n   one clause naming why the defect cannot be made unrepresentable instead\n   (stricter type, deleted path, single owning boundary) — citing the\n   `antidote` skill rather than restating it. The MINOR/`for clarity` arm\n   and trust-boundary validation are explicitly exempt.\n2. `project-trajectory/prompts/CATALOG.md` regenerated\n   (`gen_prompt_catalog.py`); the `REVIEWER` digest is the join key a\n   session log's `prompt-sha` names, so a stale catalog is a red bar.\n3. A test in `tests/test_prompts.py` pins the clause's presence, in that\n   module's existing style (it already guards 33 prompt-template\n   properties).\n4. The same discipline reaches the adjudicator briefs if and only if it\n   applies there — read `adjudicate_brief.py`'s templates before deciding;\n   do not widen by reflex, which would be this plan's own failure mode.\n5. Recorded so the effect is measurable: the fragment states the\n   structural-vs-additive remedy split of the 2026-09-01 run (1 of 13) as\n   the baseline a later sitting re-measures against.\n\n## 4. Evidence trail\n\nThe run's rounds are under `docs/reviews/wi-543-*`, `wi-552-*`, `wi-553-*`,\n`wi-563-*`, `wi-566-*`; the interplay analysis and the accretion trace are\nin the log's 2026-09-01 supervised-unpause entry and decisions 47–51. The\namendment-arm gap named in §1 step 3 is recorded there as an unfiled kit\nfinding and is NOT this row's to fix — this row changes what future rounds\nare asked to produce.\n","numLines":95,"startLine":1,"totalLines":95}}}
