{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CedJ8QjxyHrjystcubCwV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"WI-567 is complete and the branch is clean. Summary of what shipped:\n\n## WI-567 — Construction-first remedies wired into the reviewer's finding contract\n\n**The change.** `project-trajectory/prompts/reviewer.template.md`'s finding-line contract now requires, for any remedy whose concrete change **adds a check, guard, warn, or invariant**, one clause naming why the defect cannot be made *unrepresentable* instead — a stricter type, a deleted path, or a single owning boundary — **citing the vendored `antidote` skill rather than restating it** (CLAUDE.md \"Dogfood the philosophy\").\n\nIt is **warn-first by construction**: it binds the remedy's *wording*, not the verdict or any exit code — no finding is refused, downgraded, or blocked for want of the clause (plan §2, \"Not a gate\"). The **MINOR/`for clarity`** arm and validation at a **genuine trust boundary** are explicitly exempt; the target is only a guard compensating for a *reachable* bad state the design could have made unreachable.\n\n**Done-when, item by item:**\n1. ✅ Clause added to the reviewer finding contract, citing `antidote`.\n2. ✅ `prompts/CATALOG.md` regenerated — `REVIEWER` digest `5a363cd311c3` → `227c969affa9`.\n3. ✅ `tests/test_prompts.py` gains `test_the_reviewer_brief_carries_the_construction_first_clause`, pinning the clause and both exemptions in the module's existing style.\n4. ✅ **Adjudicator briefs deliberately NOT widened** — read all four `adjudicate_brief.py` templates; each rules a typed question (meaning/clarity, close disposition, queue conflict, red-TC cause), none reviews a diff and proposes a guard against a reachable bad state. Widening there is this plan's own named failure mode.\n5. ✅ Baseline recorded (log fragment + Deliverable): **1 of 13** REVIEW-A remedies structural in the 2026-09-01 run, with the three-guard successor-invariant accretion trace, for a later re-measure.\n\n**Verification.** The `check.py` commit bar passed green on both commits (prompt-catalog fresh, registry-integrity, trajectory clean — now 93% done). **pytest is not installed on this box**, so I exercised the affected test modules' exact assertions directly by loading the `prompts` module: the new clause + its exemptions, the existing reviewer bones, the `Write your verdict to (\\S+)` review-detector regex, and the single-machine-line invariant all pass. The `format` step **skipped** (ruff not importable by this interpreter — a pre-existing env condition, matching prior sessions' notes; the change is prose plus one test module, no product source).\n\n**Close ritual complete:** Deliverable filled (before Context), `specref` cleared, log fragment opens with a `## 2026-09-01 — …` heading, spec moved to `docs/archive/work/complete/` via `spec_move.py`, empty claim dir removed, and the close commit carries the `WI: WI-567` trailer. No spine rows were minted or re-statused, so no approval-brief regeneration was owed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":639,"cache_read_input_tokens":111652,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":639},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d1f7b81f-b88d-4166-875f-573dc007de72","uuid":"4c55f38d-e046-48fd-a38b-ad2303bdea58","request_id":"req_011CedJ8PoQxsm6oJerUkBnW"}
